# Fix: Fullscreen rendering — wrong positions + blurry elements

## Root Cause
`SDL_RenderSetLogicalSize(r->sdl_renderer, 1024, 768)` is set once at creation and never updated.
When the window resizes or goes fullscreen, the logical coordinate space stays at 1024x768 while
Nuklear receives the actual window size → coordinate mismatch + interpolation blur.

## Fix (1 file, ~3 lines)

### renderer.c — `renderer_update_size()`
Currently only reads `SDL_GetRendererOutputSize` for pixel dimensions.
Add: also call `SDL_RenderSetLogicalSize(r->sdl_renderer, window_w, window_h)` with the current
window size in points so that the logical coordinate space always matches the window coordinate space.

```c
void renderer_update_size(Renderer *r) {
  if (!r) return;
  int render_w, render_h;
  SDL_GetRendererOutputSize(r->sdl_renderer, &render_w, &render_h);
  r->width = render_w;
  r->height = render_h;
  // FIX: keep logical size in sync with window size
  int window_w, window_h;
  SDL_GetWindowSize(r->window, &window_w, &window_h);
  SDL_RenderSetLogicalSize(r->sdl_renderer, window_w, window_h);
}
```

This is called on every `SDL_WINDOWEVENT_RESIZED / SIZE_CHANGED / EXPOSED` (main.c:87-93).

### Why this fixes both symptoms:
- **Positioning**: Nuklear and SDL now agree on the coordinate space (window points).
- **Blur**: SDL scales from window-point resolution to pixel resolution using HiDPI (2x on Retina),
  so fonts/lines render at native pixel resolution instead of being upscaled from 1024x768.
- **Mouse**: SDL reports mouse events in logical space = window space, matching Nuklear.
